  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f4f4f4;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }
    .container {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 2rem auto;
      background: #fff;
      padding: 2rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
    }
    h1, h2 {
      color: #004080;
    }
    p {
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    ul {
      margin-left: 1.5rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .section {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    .highlight {
      background-color: #e7f3ff;
      border-left: 5px solid #007bff;
      padding: 1rem;
      margin: 1rem 0;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .img-center {
      display: block;
      margin: 2rem auto;
      max-width: 100%;
      border-radius: 6px;
    }
    a {
      color: #0066cc;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
  </style>

  <%- include('../includeFolder/_headers.ejs') %>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="container">
    <h1>JAMB <%= year %>: CBT Exam Date, Accredited Centres & Registration Requirements</h1>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>📅 JAMB CBT Exam Date <%= year %></h2>
      <p>The Joint Admissions and Matriculation Board (JAMB) schedules the annual Unified Tertiary Matriculation Examination (UTME) across accredited CBT centers nation-wide.</p>
      <p>All candidates who have successfully registered should prepare ahead and stay updated by visiting the official JAMB portal regularly.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>📍 JAMB Accredited Centres Near You</h2>
      <p>You must register and sit for your exam at JAMB-accredited centres only. These centres are authorized to ensure a secure and standardized testing experience for all candidates.</p>
      <p>To find a JAMB CBT centre near you:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Visit the official <a href="https://www.jamb.gov.ng" target="_blank">JAMB Portal</a>.</li>
        <li>Click on "Accredited CBT Centres" under the UTME menu.</li>
        <li>Select your state to view approved centres in your area.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="highlight">
        <strong>Warning:</strong> Do not register at cybercafés or unauthorized locations to avoid invalid registration or scam centers.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>📝 JAMB Registration Requirements <%= year %></h2>
      <p>Before registering for JAMB <%= year %>, ensure you have the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>NIN (National Identification Number)</strong> – Mandatory for registration.</li>
        <li><strong>Valid Email Address</strong> – Active personal email address for notifications.</li>
        <li><strong>Phone Number</strong> – Unique personal number used for profile code generation.</li>
        <li><strong>Profile Code</strong> – Generated by sending your NIN via SMS to 55019 or 66019.</li>
        <li><strong>O’Level Results (WAEC/NECO/NABTEB)</strong> – Candidates awaiting results may also apply.</li>
        <li><strong>Passport Photograph</strong> – Biometrically captured at approved CBT centers.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <img src="https://jamb.gov.ng/images/logo.png" alt="JAMB Official Logo" class="img-center" />

    <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 2rem;"><em>Stay updated, stay informed. Good luck with your JAMB <%= year %> preparation!</em></p>
  </div>

